            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Alkenes",
            "text": "Alkenes are unsaturated hydrocarbons; unsaturated hydrocarbons are compounds of hydrogen and carbon only whose molecules contain carbon-to-carbon double (or triple) bonds. Alkenes have two hydrogen atoms fewer than the corresponding saturated hydrocarbons."
          }
        ]
      }
